{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790286846,"nonce":"IdYthArZFjOu71N/MFNhzKUjfS0=","title":"HXSL: extensions for frameworks and engines","message":"The HXSL compiler need not stop at stock HXSL. A framework registers a caribou.hxsl.Extension from its library's init macro, for its shader interface or for all shaders, and adds functions (typed overloads with the WGSL a call prints), a prelude of HXSL declarations, a pass over checked shaders, WGSL for built-ins the printer lacks (Heaps' barycentrics, channels, bindless), uniform blocks and bind groups, and output roles (position, target, depth, unused). Layout constants follow blocks and groups.","files":null}]}